From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakefield kernel fixes <lakefield@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:08:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] i915/dsi: restore the Lakefield MCD D-PHY lane state

This is the change that makes the internal MIPI-DSI panel work.

Lakefield's combo PHY contains a Modular Configurable D-PHY (MCD): a
non-VPG D-PHY that does not self-configure, so software must program the
lanes (Lakefield PRM Vol 12, "MCD Programming"). i915 only knows the VPG
(Ice Lake) D-PHY, and the two register layouts alias each other: ICL's
PORT_TX_DW5 is DBBUDLN_MST_SLV_INIT_CTL here, and ICL's TX_DW writes zero
the lane TX timing registers. The D-PHY ends up with no TX timing, so no
packets leave it. A video-mode DSI panel has no link training and no
acknowledgement, so this fails completely silently.

Re-program the five lane blocks (base 0x162280 + lane * 0x200) and
CBBS_CLOCK_CTRL with the values the firmware leaves behind when the panel
is lit, after gen11_dsi_setup_dphy_timings() and before
gen11_dsi_enable_ddi_buffer(), matching the PRM order. SOFT_RST_CTL is
cleared explicitly because the swing/pre-emphasis write leaves UDLN reset
overrides there on lane 2, the clock lane.

Per-lane values matter: lane 2 is the clock lane and lane 0 is the AUX
lane, so writing lane 0's block to all five leaves the panel black.

Verified on the hardware: with this in place fb0 becomes i915drmfb, the
DSI connector is connected+enabled, and a lightdm login renders on the
panel. A firmware-vs-i915 register diff over 0x162000-0x162b3c then
agrees on all but two status registers.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/icl_dsi.c | 51 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 51 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/icl_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/icl_dsi.c
index a549f1f..fee844b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/icl_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/icl_dsi.c
@@ -1149,6 +1149,57 @@ gen11_dsi_enable_port_and_phy(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 	/* setup D-PHY timings */
 	gen11_dsi_setup_dphy_timings(encoder, crtc_state);
 
+	/*
+	 * Lakefield's D-PHY is a Modular Configurable D-PHY (MCD), a non-VPG
+	 * design with its own programming model (Lakefield PRM Vol 12, "MCD
+	 * Programming"). The ICL combo-PHY programming above lands on MCD
+	 * registers here: ICL's PORT_TX_DW5 aliases UDLN MST_SLV_INIT_CTL, and
+	 * the TX_DW writes zero DBBUDLN_TX_TIMING_CTL0/1. The lanes are then
+	 * left with no TX timing and nothing leaves the PHY - panel dark with
+	 * the backlight on, and no error anywhere because a video-mode DSI
+	 * panel has no link training and no acknowledgement.
+	 *
+	 * Restore the values the firmware programs, captured from a state in
+	 * which this panel does display (UEFI GOP, first i915 load after boot).
+	 * Lanes are NOT identical: lane 2 is the clock lane and has its own TX
+	 * timing, and lane 0 (data 0 / AUX) has TXRX_CTL bit 12 set.
+	 */
+	{
+		struct intel_display *display = to_intel_display(encoder);
+		static const struct {
+			u32 ctl, mst, t0, t1, t2, t3;
+		} mcd[5] = {
+			{ 0x00001c0b, 1, 0x08110505, 0x0a000011, 0x017f0001, 0x00030200 },
+			{ 0x00000c0b, 1, 0x08110505, 0x0a000011, 0x017f0001, 0x00030200 },
+			{ 0x00000c0b, 1, 0x08230505, 0x0a001711, 0x017f0001, 0x00030200 },
+			{ 0x00000c0b, 1, 0x08110505, 0x0a000011, 0x017f0001, 0x00030200 },
+			{ 0x00000c0b, 1, 0x08110505, 0x0a000011, 0x017f0001, 0x00030200 },
+		};
+		int lane;
+
+		/* CBBS: HS clock to left+right lanes, TX word clock /8 */
+		intel_de_write(display, _MMIO(0x162030), 0x0c518d00);
+
+		for (lane = 0; lane < 5; lane++) {
+			u32 b = 0x162280 + lane * 0x200;
+
+			/*
+			 * i915's ICL PORT_TX_DW2_GRP(PHY_A) is 0x162688, which is
+			 * this register for lane 2, and its swing/pre-emphasis
+			 * write leaves 0x18 there - the UDLN reset / TXLP latch
+			 * override bits. The firmware leaves it 0; a clock lane
+			 * held in reset means no clock and no image.
+			 */
+			intel_de_write(display, _MMIO(b + 0x08), 0x00000000);
+			intel_de_write(display, _MMIO(b + 0x10), mcd[lane].ctl);
+			intel_de_write(display, _MMIO(b + 0x14), mcd[lane].mst);
+			intel_de_write(display, _MMIO(b + 0x18), mcd[lane].t0);
+			intel_de_write(display, _MMIO(b + 0x1c), mcd[lane].t1);
+			intel_de_write(display, _MMIO(b + 0x20), mcd[lane].t2);
+			intel_de_write(display, _MMIO(b + 0x24), mcd[lane].t3);
+		}
+	}
+
 	/* enable DDI buffer */
 	gen11_dsi_enable_ddi_buffer(encoder);
 
